# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# WordPress → Astro migration map.
#
# Every URL that currently ranks or has links pointing at it must land
# somewhere sensible, or the move to Cloudflare costs you the search equity
# the old site built up. 301 (permanent) is what passes that equity on.
#
# >>> BEFORE GOING LIVE <<<
# Export the full list of live URLs from the WordPress site — Google Search
# Console › Pages, or a crawl with Screaming Frog — and add a line here for
# every one that is not already reproduced at the same path. The entries below
# cover the paths we could confirm; they are a starting point, not a complete
# map.

# --- Known WordPress paths ------------------------------------------------

# The old /medical/ page. Point this at whichever new page carries that
# content — /about/ covers guide qualifications and insurance today.
/medical            /about/                 301
/medical/*          /about/                 301

# WordPress feed and admin paths that should not 404 noisily.
/feed               /blog/                  301
/feed/*             /blog/                  301
/comments/feed      /blog/                  301
/wp-content/*       /                       301
/wp-includes/*      /                       301
/xmlrpc.php         /                       301

# WordPress date-based archives, if the blog used them.
/20:year/:month/:slug   /blog/:slug/        301

# --- Common WordPress patterns worth catching ------------------------------

/category/*         /blog/                  301
/tag/*              /blog/                  301
/author/*           /about/                 301

# --- Language paths --------------------------------------------------------
# If the WordPress site used a plugin with /en/ prefixes, English now lives at
# the root. Uncomment if that applies.
# /en/*             /:splat                 301

# --- Trailing-slash safety net ---------------------------------------------
# The site is built with trailing slashes. Cloudflare Pages normalises most of
# this automatically; these catch the main hand-typed variants.
/hikes/index        /hikes/                 301
/index.html         /                       301
